    "turn_text": "Like I said, I don't think it's merited. If they think it's merited as far as I'm concerned, go for it because I think that the checks and balances both within the FBI, with judges who have to sign off on warrants, with the FISA Court specifically, those are all areas where I think people can, as a general matter, have confidence that people did their jobs right and that there are in fact checks and balances from outside the department that are brought to bear. And I do think that the evidence that then comes to light in all of that is going to be very unflattering for the president and the administration. So I think a lot of this might be just, you know, combative talk. uh you know trash talk but not something that they truly want to pursue because if you truly get into this the evidence that emerges is probably going to reopen a lot of these issues.",
