    "turn_idx": 72,
    "turn_text": "I would have to go back and review what I've said in the past, but I would I don't recall anything that I regret at this point. I think that frankly there's an awful lot of evidence out there. And the notion that anything that anybody has said about this has been dispelled. by the Mueller report is a premature conclusion to reach until we've actually seen the Mueller report. We've just seen the bar letter about the Mueller report, and we don't yet know to my first point on the show about what the scope was of this investigation, if it was very narrowly scoped, and there are other areas that weren't looked at or where no conclusion was reached That still remains, I think, very fair game for investigation, for congressional oversight, for all those things. You know, we as members of Congress actually have an independent responsibility to engage in oversight and to disclose to the public what we're concerned about.",
